  <main id="top">
    <section class="tut-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="tut.eyebrow">The quick tour</p>
      <h1 class="tut-title" data-i18n="tut.title">How Muitra works</h1>
      <p class="tut-sub" data-i18n="tut.sub">A shared home runs on small habits. Here's the whole idea in seven short steps.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="tut-steps">
      <!-- 1 intro -->
      <article class="step">
        <div class="step-text">
          <span class="step-num">1</span>
          <span class="step-emoji">🏠</span>
          <h2 data-i18n="tutorial.intro_title">A shared home, one list.</h2>
          <p data-i18n="tutorial.intro_body">In Muitra, tasks take turns between everyone at home. Here's the quick tour.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="step-shot"><img id="t1" alt="" loading="lazy" /></figure>
      </article>

      <!-- 2 turns -->
      <article class="step">
        <div class="step-text">
          <span class="step-num">2</span>
          <span class="step-emoji">✅</span>
          <h2 data-i18n="tutorial.turns_title">Whose turn?</h2>
          <p data-i18n="tutorial.turns_body">Today shows what's yours. Tap to complete — and the turn passes to whoever's next.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="step-shot"><img id="t2" alt="" loading="lazy" /></figure>
      </article>

      <!-- 3 plan -->
      <article class="step">
        <div class="step-text">
          <span class="step-num">3</span>
          <span class="step-emoji">➕</span>
          <h2 data-i18n="tutorial.plan_title">Build your rhythm.</h2>
          <p data-i18n="tutorial.plan_body">Tap + to add a task and how often it repeats. Start a custom task's name with an emoji to spot it at a glance in the Calendar.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="step-shot"><img id="t3" alt="" loading="lazy" /></figure>
      </article>

      <!-- 4 cal -->
      <article class="step">
        <div class="step-text">
          <span class="step-num">4</span>
          <span class="step-emoji">🗓️</span>
          <h2 data-i18n="tutorial.cal_title">Two ways to look ahead.</h2>
          <p data-i18n="tutorial.cal_body">Tap Week for a day-by-day agenda, or Month for the whole picture at a glance — each task colored by who's on it.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="step-shot"><img id="t4" alt="" loading="lazy" /></figure>
      </article>

      <!-- 5 fair -->
      <article class="step">
        <div class="step-text">
          <span class="step-num">5</span>
          <span class="step-emoji">⚖️</span>
          <h2 data-i18n="tutorial.fair_title">Always fair.</h2>
          <p data-i18n="tutorial.fair_body">Muitra simply keeps turns balanced — just the two of you, or a whole household, each with their own color.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="step-shot"><img id="t5" alt="" loading="lazy" /></figure>
      </article>

    </div>

    <section class="badge-guide" id="achievements" aria-labelledby="badge-guide-title">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="badge.eyebrow">Progress</p>
      <h2 id="badge-guide-title" data-i18n="badge.title">How achievements work</h2>
      <p class="badge-guide-intro" data-i18n="badge.intro">Achievements celebrate completed tasks and the rhythm you build over time. Your private solo chapter and your household collection are counted separately.</p>
      <div class="badge-guide-grid">
        <article>
          <h3 data-i18n="badge.solo_title">Your solo chapter</h3>
          <p data-i18n="badge.solo_body">Eligible personal tasks completed while you are the only member count toward solo achievements. Completion milestones are 1, 10, 25, 100, 500 and 1,000 tasks. Rhythm badges count distinct active weeks, so a break does not erase progress.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3 data-i18n="badge.shared_title">Your household collection</h3>
          <p data-i18n="badge.shared_body">Shared progress begins when a second member joins. Eligible shared completions count once for the household. Later badges combine completion milestones with balanced weeks.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3 data-i18n="badge.balanced_title">What is a balanced week?</h3>
          <p data-i18n="badge.balanced_body">In one household-local Monday-to-Sunday week, at least 4 shared tasks must be completed by at least 2 contributors, with no one doing more than 70%. The week is counted after it ends. Balanced weeks accumulate; they do not have to be consecutive.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="get">
      <h2 data-i18n="tut.ctaTitle">Ready to try it?</h2>
      <p data-i18n="tut.ctaBody">Muitra is live on iPhone and Android. Open the download section and pick your store.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/#get" data-i18n="tut.ctaButton">Get the app</a>
    </section>
